# PATCH: 022-clear-stale-movingtab
#
# Prevents incomplete tab drags from leaving browser chrome inert.
#
# Firefox intentionally disables pointer events for most of the navigation bar
# while the navigator toolbox has the movingtab attribute. Missing dataTransfer
# objects and exceptional drag termination can skip normal cleanup and leave the
# attribute behind indefinitely, disabling the URL bar, extension buttons, and
# application menu.
#
# Each drag retains its source independently of dataTransfer so malformed drop
# and dragend events can use one complete cancellation path. That path clears
# move-together data, indices, transforms, group-drag state, indicators, and both
# movingtab markers. Cross-window cancellation uses a window-safe public entry
# point rather than a private-field call across separately evaluated classes.
#
# A toolbox mousemove watchdog recognizes either a tabstrip or toolbox marker
# once no mouse button or native drag session remains. Legitimate same-window
# drop transitions are preserved, while transitionend/transitioncancel handling
# has a bounded one-second fallback that completes the move and cleanup if the
# platform loses the terminal transition event.
#
# Firefox's navigation-bar drop shielding remains active throughout valid tab
# drags; the CSS pointer-events rule is deliberately retained.


